         "1. INNER JOIN: Returns only rows where there is a match in BOTH tables.<br>2. LEFT (OUTER) JOIN: Returns ALL rows from the left table, along with matching rows from the right table. For left rows with no match on the right, NULL values are filled in right-table columns.<br>3. RIGHT (OUTER) JOIN: Returns all rows from the right table, and matching rows from the left table (symmetric opposite of Left Join).<br>4. FULL OUTER JOIN: Returns all rows when there is a match in either table. If there is no match on one side, NULLs are populated.<br>5. CROSS JOIN (Cartesian Product): Produces every combination of rows from Table A with Table B. If Table A has M rows and Table B has N rows, output has M * N rows (no ON condition).",
